course: dictionary
lesson: 6967
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning is right. The first meaning of pancake is a thin, flat, round cake made from batter of flour, eggs and milk, cooked in a frying pan. «Gareth makes Leon pancakes every Saturday» tells you pancakes are food.
explain: The second meaning is in the phrase «flat as a pancake», which means very flat. If a sentence says a field is flat as a pancake, the word is not about food at all. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit this sentence? If not, try the other meaning.
explain: Some pancakes are thin and some are thick. «American pancakes are thick and small; British ones are thin like crêpes.» Context clues like these help you picture the food and understand the word.
fact: A pancake is a thin, flat, round cake cooked in a frying pan.
fact: A pancake is made from batter of flour, eggs and milk.
fact: «Flat as a pancake» means very flat.
fact: In Britain, Ireland and some parts of Australia, families eat pancakes on Pancake Day, also called Shrove Tuesday.
fact: «Mlyntsi» are thin Ukrainian pancakes, eaten with jam or cottage cheese.
exercise: What is a pancake? | A sweet sauce poured over ice cream | A thick, tall cake baked in an oven | A small bread roll | *A thin, flat, round cake cooked in a frying pan
exercise: «The field was flat as a pancake.» What does this phrase mean? | Very round | *Very flat | Very tall | Very wet
exercise: «In Brittany une crêpe is a thin, usually sweet pancake.» Find and copy one word that describes the shape of a crêpe. | *thin | usually | Brittany | sweet
test: «Mlyntsi are thin pancakes eaten with jam or cottage cheese.» What are mlyntsi eaten with? | Ice cream and chips | *Jam or cottage cheese | Syrup and lemon only | Salt and pepper
test: British pancakes are thin, like which French food? | Pizza | *Crêpes | Croissants | Baguettes
exam: «American pancakes are thick and small; British ones are thin like crêpes.» What is the difference between them? | Both are made without eggs | *American pancakes are thick and small; British ones are thin | Both are thin and very large | American pancakes are thin; British ones are thick
